# This repository tracks the tool, never the fleet's own data.
# Anything naming real hosts, users, addresses, or credentials stays local.
# Sanitized stand-ins for every ignored file live in examples/.
#
# Leading slashes anchor these to the repository root, so the copies under
# examples/ are still tracked.

# Credentials and identifying values.
/.env
/.env.opencode

# Live inventory: real hostnames and SSH users.
# Stand-in: examples/inventory.json
/inventory.json

# Generated from the live inventory.
# Stand-ins: examples/devices.md, examples/coding-agents-cli.md
/devices.md
/coding-agents-cli.md

# Dated run logs: hostnames, usernames, resolved paths.
# Stand-in: examples/logs/
/logs/

# Host-specific service runbooks: addresses, unit paths, home directories.
/docs/services/

# Runtime lock created by ./fleet to serialize log writes.
/.fleet.lock

# Python bytecode.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
